  const FAM = '<h4 class="art-h">Modern families in the UK</h4><p>There are 19.2 million families in the UK. These families are couples with or without children and single-parent families.</p><p>Many homes have got parents with grown-up children in their 20s and 30s. Often, they are at home until they are married (the average age for men is 38 years old and women is 35).</p><p>Couples are usually engaged for 20 months.</p><p>Houses are expensive in the UK. Many families haven’t got a lot of money for their own home. Sometimes an “extended” family (aunts, uncles, nieces, nephews, grandparents, grandchildren, etc.) lives in one house.</p><p>The typical family has got 1.89 children.</p><p>Today, many couples haven’t got children. Sometimes, it’s a choice – because their work is important or because they haven’t got time.</p><p>But one thing is the same every year: for every 100 girls, there are 105.4 boys.</p>';
