  const PROP = '<p><b>Room in 5 bedroom house to rent</b> · £530 a month · Welby Avenue, Lenton, Nottingham · 11 months from September 1st</p><h4 class="art-h">Property details</h4><p><mark>Downstairs</mark> there is a large, comfortable <mark>living room</mark>, a <mark>dining room</mark>, a <mark>study</mark>, and a <mark>kitchen</mark>. There is a large <mark>hall</mark>. There’s also a <mark>basement</mark>.</p><p><mark>Upstairs</mark> there are three <mark>bedrooms</mark>, a <mark>toilet</mark> and there’s another bedroom in the <mark>attic</mark>. There’s a <mark>bathroom</mark> with a bath and shower.</p><p>The house is near Nottingham University and there are a lot of shops and cafés nearby. It is a perfect home for students.</p>';
  const HK = '<h4 class="art-h">A DIFFERENT LIFE</h4><p><b>Family homes are different sizes in different places. Hong Kong is a small city, but it’s got a large population. This means homes are very small, as well as expensive. Some people sleep with the washing machine under their bed, or next to the cooker. So how do they find a nice home? Anthony Chan, 16, has a solution.</b></p><p>“I live with my parents on a houseboat. It doesn’t cost a lot of money and it’s got a lot of space. In addition, it’s quiet, but it’s near my school as well as shops. I walk to school every day. I love our boat, especially the kitchen: it’s big, with an enormous fridge full of all my favourite food! Our living room is also big with a soft carpet, sofas, armchairs, bookcases, and lamps. Mum spends a lot of time in there. My dad also loves our boat because he enjoys life outside on the water as well as inside the boat.</p><p>Most families don’t live on houseboats. There isn’t much space for them. However, a lot of families want this life. I hope it’s possible for them in the future.”</p>';
  const ROOMS = ['attic', 'basement', 'bathroom', 'bedroom', 'dining room', 'downstairs', 'hall', 'kitchen', 'living room', 'study', 'toilet', 'upstairs'];
